WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.060
- Big news outta the Supreme Court!

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.890
There is nothing standing in the way

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.350
of New York prosecutors getting

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.790
former President Donald Trump's taxes

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:10.780
for purposes of a criminal investigation.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.780
Recently the Supreme Court
denied a stay request from Trump.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.310
Basically, this is the whole game,

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.510
it's not about a decision on the merits.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.420
The Trump camp wanted to prevent

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.140
the New York prosecutors
from getting his taxes

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.230
while the Supreme Court
was figuring all this out.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.167
And the Supreme court says,

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:29.130
"No, we will not stay things,
things will go forward,"

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.530
and now the New York
prosecutors should be able

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.850
to get access to former
President Trump's taxes.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.200
And that's a big deal because Mazers,

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.530
the accounting firm that
was holding these records,

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.570
has wanted to comply with prosecutors,

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:40.750
so there's nothing that stops them

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.490
from handing those over to
the prosecutors immediately.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.080
And that's continual bad
news for the Trump camp

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.680
because New York prosecutors
just signed up Mark Pomerantz,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.200
who is a former federal prosecutor

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.110
who appears to be an expert in these kind

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.130
of white collar tax-related crimes.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.130
So let's see what happens.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.390
And if you were a member
of the Trump organization,

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.483
I may actually see you in court.

